from authoring import finish,ref,step,paragraph
finish('internal-semisimplicial-types-in-ordinary-hott',
 id='TCS-6569',title='An internal tower of semisimplicial types in ordinary HoTT',area='Semantics, logic and verification',criterion='construction',question_type='yes_no',
 formal='In the fixed ordinary HoTT theory T below, can one define a single internal family S:ℕ→U₁ and restriction maps r_n:S(n+1)→S(n) whose finite stages are equivalent, compatibly with restriction, to the canonical finite semisimplicial telescopes D_n?',
 definitions='Fix T to be intensional Martin–Löf type theory with dependent function and pair types Π,Σ, identity types with their J eliminator, empty and unit types, finite coproducts, natural numbers and W-types, a cumulative predicative sequence U₀:U₁:⋯ closed under these constructors, and univalence for these universes. Also allow propositional truncation and homotopy pushouts with their ordinary dependent eliminators and propositional computation rules for path constructors, as in the HoTT book. There is no equality reflection, axiom K/UIP, resizing, choice, excluded middle, second equality type, display modality, or additional primitive for semisimplicial types. The question concerns definability in this specified theory; a negative result would apply to this theory, not automatically to every possible extension called HoTT. Define an external, finite family of syntactic telescopes as follows. D₀ is U₀, with element A₀. Given data d=(A₀,…,A_{j−1}) in D_{j−1}, form B_j(d), the dependent type of labelled boundaries of a j-simplex: for every nonempty proper subset F of {0,…,j}, in increasing cardinality and then lexicographic order, choose a label x_F in A_{|F|−1} evaluated on the labels of all nonempty proper subfaces of F. Identify F with {0,…,|F|−1} by its increasing enumeration when supplying these arguments. For singleton F this means x_F:A₀. Set D_j=Σ(d:D_{j−1})(B_j(d)→U₀), whose last field is A_j, and let p_j:D_{j+1}→D_j forget the last field. This describes an ordinary finite T-expression for each external integer j; it does not postulate an internal function j↦D_j. The required output is finite closed T-terms S:ℕ→U₁ and r:Π(n:ℕ)(S(n+1)→S(n)), together with a metatheoretic proof that for every external j there are T-terms e_j:S(j)≃D_j and homotopies e_j∘r_j ~ p_j∘e_{j+1}. Here j inside T denotes its numeral, ≃ is the usual type equivalence, and ~ is pointwise identity. No judgmental equality between S(j) and D_j is required. The equivalences classify the full type-valued telescopes, with arbitrary U₀-small simplex types and no fixed truncation bound.',
 answer_criterion='Construct the finite terms S,r and prove the stated compatible stage-equivalence property for all external dimensions, or prove that no such terms and equivalences exist in T. A metaprogram that emits a different telescope for each numeral is already available and is insufficient. Defining only set-valued semisimplicial objects, finitely many dimensions, or a construction in an enriched theory does not settle this particular target. Given S and r, the ordinary sequential homotopy limit Σ(a:Πn S(n))Πn(r_n(a(n+1))=a(n)) is the associated internal type of compatible infinite data.',
 context=[
 paragraph('Homotopy type theory treats identity as mathematical data that can itself have nontrivial identities. This makes it a natural setting for spaces and higher structures, but it changes what it means to give a diagram. In set-level mathematics, equations between composites can be recorded once and used without further information. For general types, chosen identifications can have multiple distinct witnesses, and comparisons between those witnesses may matter in the next dimension.','book'),
 paragraph('A semisimplicial type begins with a type A₀ of vertices. For every ordered pair of vertices, A₁ gives a type of edges. For every triangle boundary—three vertices and three specified edges—A₂ gives a type of fillers. At dimension three, a filler is indexed by four vertices, six edges and four triangular fillers sharing their appropriate faces. Nothing forces a filler to exist, and the type of fillers may itself have arbitrarily rich homotopy.'),
 paragraph('The finite telescope description records shared boundaries through dependent types. A triangle’s three edges are already assigned the required endpoints; one does not choose unrelated edges and then append a collection of endpoint equations. The same idea works at each externally fixed dimension. The difficulty is making the whole construction into one function that accepts an internal natural number, rather than a growing list of separately written definitions.'),
 paragraph('This is why the card distinguishes its externally specified D_j from the sought internal S. A script can generate the expression for D_100 and a type checker can check it. That does not supply a HoTT term whose argument is an arbitrary n:ℕ. The compatibility requirement also matters: a collection of unrelated types with the right apparent sizes would not tell us how to forget the highest-dimensional data.'),
 paragraph('The statement deliberately allows equivalence at each stage instead of demanding a particular syntactic normal form. Thus a clever alternative encoding can solve the problem if it represents all the prescribed data and respects truncation. Once the internal tower exists, dependent sums, products and identity types already express a compatible infinite sequence. The missing step is constructing the tower itself, not adding a primitive that merely asserts an infinite sequence exists.'),
 paragraph('Kraus’s TYPES 2018 discussion identifies uniform finite-dimensional semisimplicial types as a major open problem and explains their role in higher category theory. Adding suitable Segal and completeness conditions to such data provides a route toward internal higher categories. Those conditions are additional structure: this card asks first for unrestricted semisimplicial data, with no composition, identity or horn-filling axioms imposed.','primary'),
 paragraph('Two-level type theory introduces an outer equality satisfying uniqueness of identity proofs, alongside the homotopical inner theory. It can formalize constructions indexed by outer natural numbers. Annenkov, Capriotti, Kraus and Sattler distinguish this from constructing an inner universe of infinite semisimplicial types; additional hypotheses relating the two natural-number objects support the latter. The May 2026 revision is labelled a typo and reference update, not a new solution in ordinary HoTT.','twolevel'),
 paragraph('Displayed Type Theory takes another route. Kolomatskaia and Shulman introduce discrete and simplicial modes together with a primitive display operation, then use it for a coinductive construction of semisimplicial types. This is a substantive solution in their enriched system, with a detailed semantic correctness argument. It does not give a definition from the constructors of T alone, because those additional primitives are precisely what enable the construction.','displayed'),
 paragraph('Chen’s 2025 thesis studies internal models and Reedy-fibrant inverse diagrams directly. It explicitly retains the ordinary-HoTT semisimplicial problem as open. Section 6.1 labels its proposed classifier construction a sketch whose Agda formalization has unresolved termination and definitional-equality issues, and states that it is not intended to solve the unrestricted problem. This is useful progress toward articulating the required coherence, rather than a completed internal classifier.','chen'),
 paragraph('A set-valued construction also does not suffice. If every simplex type is a set, identities between elements have no higher ambiguity, and ordinary categorical equations behave much more rigidly. The requirement that the simplex types range over U₀ preserves the higher-dimensional content that motivates the problem. Likewise, having a satisfactory semantic construction in a model does not automatically produce a finite term definable in the specified syntax.'),
 paragraph('A positive answer would show that ordinary dependent types can organize this fundamental form of unbounded coherence without additional structure in the language. A negative answer would identify a precise expressive limitation and help explain why successful alternative foundations introduce new primitives. Either outcome would guide the design of proof assistants intended to support higher category theory and internal constructions of type-theoretic models.')],
 why='Determine whether ordinary HoTT can express a fundamental unbounded coherent structure internally, a basic issue for higher categories and foundational proof languages.',
 importance=dict(score=95,method='editorial',assessed_on='2026-09-11',reason='A central expressiveness problem for homotopy type theory; precise internal construction would remove a major obstacle to formalizing higher structures without enriching the theory.'),
 progress=[step('2013','The HoTT book supplies the ordinary dependent-type, univalence and higher-inductive framework fixed for this card.','book'),step('2018','Kraus states the uniform finite-level semisimplicial family problem and explains its connection to higher categories and internal metatheory.','primary'),step('2023','Annenkov and coauthors develop the two-level framework and distinguish outer-indexed constructions from inner semisimplicial universes.','ref2'),step('2025','Chen’s thesis develops internal-model methods but explicitly marks the classifier construction incomplete and the unrestricted ordinary-HoTT problem open.','chen'),step('2025-12-17','The journal version of Displayed Type Theory gives semisimplicial types using additional modal/display primitives; the preprint dates from 2023–2024.','displayed'),step('2026-05-26','Two-Level Type Theory v5 updates typos and references while retaining the distinction between ordinary HoTT and enriched constructions.','twolevel')],
 references=[ref('primary','On the Role of Semisimplicial Types','Nicolai Kraus',2018,'https://nicolaikraus.github.io/docs/on_semisimplicial_types.pdf','Inherited reference; TYPES 2018 talk abstract, pp. 1–2; explicitly asks for one N-indexed family rather than separately constructed finite stages'),ref('book','Homotopy Type Theory: Univalent Foundations of Mathematics','The Univalent Foundations Program',2013,'https://homotopytypetheory.org/book/','Chapters 1–2, 5–6 and Appendix A; rules for the constructors explicitly selected in the theory T on this card'),ref('ref2','Two-level type theory and applications','Danil Annenkov; Paolo Capriotti; Nicolai Kraus; Christian Sattler',2023,'https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/mathematical-structures-in-computer-science/article/twolevel-type-theory-and-applications/4914DB4F8E8305DFC68F9CDCA9D0C8D0','Inherited reference; Mathematical Structures in Computer Science 33, 688–743; introduction and Reedy-diagram constructions'),ref('twolevel','Two-Level Type Theory and Applications — revised manuscript','Danil Annenkov; Paolo Capriotti; Nicolai Kraus; Christian Sattler',2026,'https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.03307v5','First posted 2017, journal 2023; v5 dated 26 May 2026, described as a typo fix and reference update; introduction distinguishes inner and outer indexing'),ref('displayed','Displayed type theory and semi-simplicial types','Astra Kolomatskaia; Michael Shulman',2025,'https://doi.org/10.1017/S096012952510025X','MSCS 35, e34, published online 17 December 2025; arXiv:2311.18781v2, 1 February 2024; display primitive, coinductive definition and semantic correctness'),ref('chen','Internal Constructions in Homotopical Type Theory','Joshua Chen',2025,'https://www.joshchen.io/pdf/thesis-phd.pdf','PhD thesis; Sections 4.4, 6.1 and 6.3; 4.4*17 retains the open problem, 6.1*2–3 mark the construction a sketch and delimit its scope')],
 status='source_open',status_note='No internal construction or nondefinability theorem satisfying this precise tower criterion in T was found through 11 September 2026. Two-level and displayed type theories add structure beyond T; Chen’s thesis explicitly reports an incomplete classifier construction. The fixed theory and compatible finite-stage criterion replace the otherwise ambiguous phrase “in ordinary HoTT.”',formulation_reviewed_on='2026-09-11')
